# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caddyfile — Yield Portal reverse proxy (internal LAN)
#
# Role: take browser requests on port 80 (any hostname: the FQDN
#       yieldportal.socionext.com, the Windows computer name, or the IP)
#       and forward them to the FastAPI app listening on 127.0.0.1:8000.
#
# The app (uvicorn) is bound to 127.0.0.1 so it is NOT reachable from the
# network directly — only Caddy is. See docs/deploy-windows.md for setup.
#
# Run:   caddy run --config Caddyfile
# (or install as a Windows service via NSSM — see the runbook.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Listen on port 80 for ALL hostnames. Plain HTTP (no certificate needed).
# Works the moment IT points yieldportal.socionext.com at this machine's IP.
:80 {
	encode zstd gzip

	# Forward everything to the FastAPI app.
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000

	# Optional: write access logs to a file.
	log {
		output file C:\caddy\logs\access.log {
			roll_size 10MiB
			roll_keep 5
		}
	}
}

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LATER — when you want HTTPS (https://yieldportal.socionext.com)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Replace the `:80 { ... }` block above with ONE of the following.
#
# ── Option A: Caddy's own internal CA (no internet, no IT cert needed) ──
#   Caddy generates a local certificate automatically. Each client PC must
#   trust Caddy's root CA once (export it and have IT push it, or install
#   manually). Good for LAN-only HTTPS.
#
#     yieldportal.socionext.com {
#         tls internal
#         encode zstd gzip
#         reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
#     }
#
# ── Option B: a certificate issued by your corporate CA ──
#   Ask IT for a cert + key for yieldportal.socionext.com, save them on the
#   machine, and point Caddy at the files. Browsers trust it with no warning
#   because the corporate root CA is already on managed PCs.
#
#     yieldportal.socionext.com {
#         tls C:\caddy\certs\yieldportal.crt C:\caddy\certs\yieldportal.key
#         encode zstd gzip
#         reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
#     }
#
# ── LATER — simple access control (Basic auth) ──
#   Generate a password hash:  caddy hash-password
#   Then add inside the site block:
#
#     basicauth {
#         # username  <hash from "caddy hash-password">
#         viewer  $2a$14$....................................................
#     }
